{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_project_guidance", "label": "CLAUDE.md Project Guidance", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_gatekeeper_project", "label": "Gatekeeper Project (fork lineage & maintenance mode)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GatekeeperV3.1 is a fork of leonbreidenbach-pc/GatekeeperV3, itself a fork of k8thekat/GatekeeperV2; it is in maintenance mode, not active feature development, aside from the specific fork deltas listed in README.md."}, {"id": "claude_amp_integration_layer", "label": "AMP Integration Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_discord_bot_layer", "label": "Discord Bot Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_i18n_system", "label": "Internationalization (i18n) System", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gatekeeper supports English/German as a single global language switchable at runtime by an admin, not per-user Discord client locale; live switching mutates already-registered command/param descriptions and Choice.name via discord.py internals, guarded by a length check for Discord's 1-100 char limit."}, {"id": "claude_database_layer", "label": "Database Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_whitelist_only_verification", "label": "-whitelist-only Flag Needs Live Verification", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "perms_whitelist_only() deliberately grants no ADS.* node; it's undocumented whether AMP's ADSModule/GetInstances requires one, so a fresh -whitelist-only restart could lose instance visibility entirely if it turns out to need one - must be live-tested before production use."}, {"id": "claude_production_deployment_hetzner", "label": "Production Deployment Log (Hetzner, fullsendhub.de)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First real-world deployment of this fork; nearly every fix traced back to the target server running Python 3.13 (not the README's assumed 3.11) combined with a newer CubeCoders AMP build than originally tested against."}, {"id": "claude_amp_role_permission_bootstrap_bug", "label": "AMP Bot Role/Permission Bootstrap Ordering Bug", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "setup_AMPbotrole() joined the bot to the still-empty Gatekeeper role before setup_Gatekeeper_Permissions() set any permission on it; AMP resolves permissions as a union across roles with deny beating allow, so joining an unconfigured role cancelled the bot's own Super Admin grant mid-setup. Fixed by configuring permissions first, then joining the role."}, {"id": "claude_loopback_investigation", "label": "AMP Loopback Reachability False Lead", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Originally attributed to AMP requiring the public domain over loopback, but that was a false lead caused by bad/mistyped credentials in the original curl test; loopback (http://127.0.0.1:8080) works fine and is now used, removing an unnecessary round trip to the public internet for every AMP API call."}, {"id": "claude_http_session_reuse", "label": "AMP HTTP Session Reuse (requests.Session())", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CallAPI() previously opened a brand-new requests.post() per call with no connection reuse; switched to a single shared AMPHandler.http_session = requests.Session() reused across the main instance and all per-server AMPInstances, pooling TCP/TLS connections since they all target the same AMP host."}, {"id": "claude_escape_markdown_lesson", "label": "Escape External Text Before Embed Markdown Interpolation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/link steam and /link minecraft interpolated unescaped Steam personaname/Minecraft IGN into markdown (clickable link / bold text); a rogue underscore or other markdown special char in a display name would partially misrender as emphasis. Fixed via discord.utils.escape_markdown() on the display text only, preserving the clickable link."}, {"id": "claude_subcommand_lesson", "label": "Per-Lookup-Type Commands Need Subcommands, Not Enum Param", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/user info used one command with an identifier_type Choice plus two always-visible params; Discord slash commands cannot conditionally show/hide a parameter based on another parameter's value, so both fields always showed regardless of type picked. Split into /user info discord|minecraft|steam subcommands, each exposing only its relevant required param."}, {"id": "claude_permission_node_drift", "label": "AMP Permission Node Drift Reconciliation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "perms_super()/perms_whitelist_only() reconciled against a live Core/GetPermissionsSpec dump: 4 stale/renamed nodes fixed (including a lost LocalFileBackup.* grant with no modern equivalent found), plus several wildcard-granted-but-unused nodes excluded (Store.*, ADS.DatastoreManagement.*, unused Settings.* category, etc.)."}, {"id": "claude_python313_compatibility_fixes", "label": "Python 3.13 Bootstrap Compatibility Fixes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Server runs Python 3.13, which broke pip install (stale requirements.txt pins), haggis's private-lock-based logging monkeypatch, and discord.py's audioop import; a batch of one-fix-per-commit changes across requirements.txt/AMP.py/logger.py/amp_permissions.py restored a working bootstrap."}, {"id": "claude_amp_handler", "label": "AMP_Handler.py (AMPHandler singleton)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_amp_instance", "label": "AMP.py (AMPInstance base class)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_discordbot", "label": "discordBot.py (Gatekeeper bot class)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_loader", "label": "loader.py (extension/cog auto-loader)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_db", "label": "DB.py (Database wrapper)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_db_update", "label": "DB_Update.py (versioned DB migrations)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_amp_permissions", "label": "amp_permissions.py (AMP permission profiles)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_start", "label": "start.py (Setup / startup sequence)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_logger", "label": "logger.py (logging configuration)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_amp_user_info_crash_fix", "label": "Core.UserManagement.ViewUserInfo Self-Check Crash Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "check_GatekeeperRole_Permissions()'s self-lookup (Core/GetAMPUserInfo) was rejected with Unauthorized Access on a per-instance delegate session even though node-based permission checks had just passed; unhandled indexing of the False result threw a TypeError that killed the AMP Handler thread. Fixed by checking isinstance(result, dict) before indexing, treating a rejected self-lookup as a non-fatal warning for InstanceID != 0 while keeping it critical for the main instance."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_project_guidance", "target": "claude_gatekeeper_project", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_project_guidance", "target": "claude_amp_integration_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_project_guidance", "target": "claude_discord_bot_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_project_guidance", "target": "claude_i18n_system", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_project_guidance", "target": "claude_database_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_project_guidance", "target": "claude_production_deployment_hetzner", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_amp_integration_layer", "target": "claude_amp_handler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_amp_integration_layer", "target": "claude_amp_instance", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_amp_integration_layer", "target": "claude_whitelist_only_verification", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file":